# Task: Create or Update Agent Rules

## When to Use

Trigger this rule via @-mention when creating a new agent rule document or updating an existing one in `functions/docs/`. These files are loaded at runtime by the JS prompt builders in `functions/prompts/` and directly control agent behaviour.

## Instructions

1. Read `functions/docs/agent_architecture.md` for the canonical agent roster and Maker-Checker loop requirements.
2. Read `knowledge/fca-regulations.md` to ensure the document includes FCA compliance constraints.
3. If updating an existing file, read the current version first and preserve its structure.
4. Save the document to `functions/docs/`.

## Existing Agent Rule Files

| File | Agent | Purpose |
|------|-------|---------|
| `functions/docs/compliance_rules.md` | Compliance Agent | FCA Consumer Duty validation rules |
| `functions/docs/design_guidelines.md` | Design Agent | Visual asset prompting rules and constraints |
| `functions/docs/telemetry_rules.md` | Telemetry Agent | Micro and macro data triggers |
| `functions/docs/financial_standards.md` | Creator Agent | PISA financial literacy pillars and topic boundaries |
| `functions/docs/lesson_guidelines.md` | Creator Agent | Mobile screen constraints, tone, and JSON output rules |
| `functions/docs/agent_architecture.md` | All | System-wide pipeline architecture |

## Naming Convention

Use descriptive `snake_case` names ending in `.md` (e.g., `personalisation_rules.md`, `quiz_difficulty_rules.md`).

## Quality Checklist

- The document states clear, positive rules (what the agent MUST do) and prohibitions (what it MUST NEVER do).
- FCA compliance constraints are included where the agent handles user-facing content.
- The language is concise and scannable -- the AI agent reads this at runtime.
- Word limits and design constraints reference `03-design-system.mdc` where applicable.
